00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:38.860
The technique re-parameterizes generation as learning of velocity field that transports noise to

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:45.220
data along straight paths in probability space. The model therefore predicts the instantaneous

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:51.660
direction of the probability flow rather than a score or noise estimate. Straight paths let the

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:57.380
Odesimal Disciver Solver take larger steps at inference time and cut the number of function

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:03.920
evaluations required. Training pays a cost because the velocity target must be estimated from paired

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:09.640
noise data points, which raises gradient variance compared with the simpler noise prediction loss.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:17.360
In the min-flx loop, the VAE first encodes images, the flow matching velocity is computed,

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:24.480
and an MSE loss regresses against that velocity. Choose flow matching when your inference budget is

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:30.720
dominated by solver steps. Stick with classic diffusion when training stability matters more than

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:37.500
step count. Try the virtual's plus latent integration if you already run agents that need fast GLM

